    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "The Entity List is an export control policy used to prevent certain foreign “entities” (firms, universities, etc.) from acquiring sensitive American technology. In recent years, the Entity List has increasingly been used against firms in the People’s Republic of China (PRC). Yet researchers have not adequately measured how Entity List placement affects the overall financial performance of sanctioned PRC firms. This thesis estimates the effect of Entity List placement on the financial performance of publicly traded PRC firms added to the Entity List from 2018 to 2021. Across all cohorts (a firm’s cohort is the year it was sanctioned), Entity List placement does not have a statistically significant (at a 5% significance level) impact on sanctioned firms’ revenue, annual revenue growth, assets, employee count, gross margin, operating margin, R&D spending, R&D intensity (R&D spending / revenue), foreign revenue, and foreign sales ratio (foreign revenue / total revenue). I also estimate cohort-specific effects and find that Entity List placement does not have a statistically significant (at a 5% significance level) impact on the 2018, 2019, and 2021 cohorts. In the 2020 cohort, Entity List placement is associated with slight declines in assets, employee count, and R&D spending, but I show that these effects are driven by an outlier firm whose negative performance is unrelated to the Entity List. Thus, my overall finding is that Entity List placement does not have a significant impact on the financial performance of publicly traded PRC firms. Next, using evidence from firms’ public filings, I argue that these results are primarily driven by two mechanisms: firms’ lack of exposure to American inputs and firms’ effective substitution of American inputs. Policymakers should consider that these mechanisms may reduce the Entity List’s effectiveness against PRC firms.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
